Al-Ḥārith ibn Murra ibn Dūdān al-Nufaylī. He lived into the Islamic period. Wathīma mentioned him in his account of the apostasy and quoted an admonition that he delivered to the Banū ʿĀmir, including:

‘Banū ʿĀmir, if you support God, you will be supported;
if you oppose God and the religion, you will be forsaken.

If you are routed, no escape will save you from Him;
and if you stand firm before the people, by God, you will be killed.’

Ibn Fatḥūn and Ibn al-Amīn also added him to the earlier works.

Al-Rabīʿ ibn Aws ibn al-Aʿwar ibn Shaybān ibn ʿAmr ibn Jābir ibn ʿUqayl ibn Mālik ibn Shamkh ibn Fazāra al-Fazārī, a poet who lived through both the pre-Islamic and Islamic periods. Al-Marzubānī mentioned him and quoted these lines of his:

Your father is of Muzayna, without doubt;
Can the signs of daylight be concealed?
